    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email-uniqueness rejection for owner creation, mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern. The `POST /api/owners` pipeline already lower-cases the email in `ValidateNewOwner`, so I added a validation gate step right after the telephone check.\n\nNew/changed files:\n\n- **`ValidateUniqueEmail.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs after `ValidateNewOwner` (email already lower-cased) and before `BuildOwner`. Skips the check when email is absent (never a conflict); otherwise scans existing owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` if any owner's normalized (lower-cased) email matches.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new, checked exception) \u2014 so it appears in the `throws` clause.\n- **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** (new) \u2014 responds `409 Conflict`.\n- **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** (new escalation) \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `uniqueEmail` step between `uniqueTelephone` and `uniqueHousehold`, before any entity is built or persisted.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (and the full suite) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
