        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a faithful, additive parallel of the existing telephone-uniqueness feature, and it lands in exactly the right units:\n\n- `DuplicateEmailException` / `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler` mirror `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler` one-for-one (checked exception, 409 handler with `ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<Void>>`), so a maintainer sees the established escalation shape.\n- `ValidateUniqueEmail` mirrors `ValidateUniqueTelephone`: same `service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto, OwnerRepository)` signature, same gate-only \"publishes nothing, escalates on conflict\" role, same Javadoc idiom. It correctly reuses `OwnerEmail.normalize` (the documented single source of truth) rather than re-implementing lower-casing, matching how the telephone gate reuses `OwnerTelephone.normalize`.\n- The optional-email null guard is a justified, minimal deviation from the telephone gate (telephone is required, email isn't), and the comment states the intent.\n- YAML wiring is consistent: the new step slots between `uniqueTelephone` and `uniqueHousehold` with correct `next:` chaining, before any entity is built or persisted, and the escalation YAML follows the fully-qualified-name convention.\n\nNo duplication, nothing becoming a catch-all, logic is at the right altitude."
